From: Emre Yavuzalp <emreyavuzalp@gmail.com>
Subject: econet-eth: compute the engine slot from the descriptor (O(1), drop scan)

The bind logs revealed the descriptor was telling us the slot all along, just
scaled: real_slot = hw_slot * 2 / 5 (engine slot 16/2736/1776/1804 vs descriptor
hw_slot 40/6840/4440/4510 - exactly x2.5, because the ppe_entry field counts in
32-byte units and a FOE entry is 80 bytes). The full-table scan was only needed
because we did not know this relation; under a many-flow speed test the scan ran
in softirq for every unbound flow and pinned the CPU at 75% sirq / 0% idle.

Compute the slot directly and verify the one candidate; fall back to the scan
only if it does not match (rare). This makes binding O(1) and frees the CPU so
bound flows actually reach line rate.

diff -ruN b133/econet_ppe_offload.c b134/econet_ppe_offload.c
--- a/econet_ppe_offload.c	2026-06-29 23:47:35.200146752 +0300
+++ b/econet_ppe_offload.c	2026-06-29 23:48:08.846331453 +0300
@@ -537,47 +537,70 @@
